<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#mehri-language">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mehri language</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mehri is a Modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-arabia">South Arabian</a> language spoken by the Mahra people of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a> and western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oman">Oman</a>, and by migrants in the Gulf states. It is a Semitic language but not a form of Arabic, being descended from languages spoken in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a> before the spread of Arabic. It is mostly unwritten and has well over 100,000 speakers.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mehri-language.jpg" alt="Mehri language" width="320" height="377" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ArnoldPlaton · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Modern_South_Arabian_Languages_(cropped).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
